# Regenerable analysis output. Screenshots and the progress page stay tracked
# because they are the record the critics judged; these are not.
#   sessions:  npx tsx tools/analysis/run-pipeline.ts <track> <seed> <laps>
#   raw runs:  npx tsx tools/analysis/dump-run.ts <track> <seed> <laps>
artifacts/*.json

# EVERY subdirectory of artifacts/ is an agent's private working space unless it is named below.
#
# This started as `artifacts/critic-*/` and then chased a prefix at a time — a private dist, a
# per-agent shots directory, then a wave of agents that happened to be called "judge" instead of
# "critic" and slipped straight through. A rule keyed on what a directory is CALLED loses to the
# next person who picks a different word, so this one is keyed on what it IS: scratch, unless it
# is part of the record.
#
# The record is: `shots/` and `video/` (what the harness captures and what critics read as
# evidence), `audio/` (the rendered waveform sheet the sound design cites), `progress.html`, and
# the plots at the top level. Anything an agent wants judged or kept goes in one of those.
artifacts/*/
!artifacts/shots/
!artifacts/video/
!artifacts/audio/
# ...but a capture directory nested inside a kept one is still scratch.
artifacts/audio/*/
